Political Flame Wars - just say no! this is serious flame-bait (wildly 
and wilfully misinterpret what I say, then say how stupid of me it was to say
it). I think that I'll just stick my fingers in my ears and say 'I'm not
listening!' over and over again in a whining voice. The rest of the list will
thank me for it. Tim, if you object to my characterisation of this post, why
not hassle me over email (davidc@cs.uwa.edu.au).

	What I said was that people who believe in the right to criticise the
government as important, shouldn't be quite so agressive against just because
they do so. And as Chomsky points out, the eason he directs so much criticism
against the US is because in most ways he sees it as being more advanced - the
model much of the world is aiming for, and one where he can make his criticisms 
count for something.Hardly a red-blooded socialist point of view. Chomsky is
not someone who can be just ignored because of his left wing tendencies. He
appears on mainstream media in the rest of the world quite a lot, if not in the
US. Ignore him if you wish, but I it will only conform my suspicion that
political close mindedness is not just rampant but extreme among parts of this
list (not all). It doesn't bother me if you are Right wing, but to 
contemptuously dismiss someone as smart as Chomsky because he is more associate
