 What is it going to do with this multi-gigabyte database? With today's
processing power about all that I can imagine is that it would select nearly
random examples from the database or take months to access anything in a
semi-intelligent way.
 If I had a few teraflops, I have some ideas about how to organize the
database and access it well enough to simulate human intelligence.

 Eliza-type programs can look good if you restrict the subject enough, but
try discussing something which requires a fair amount of real world knowledge
(say PPL, uploading, or cryptography) and their limitations will become
obvious. There may be a few suckers who can't resist arguing with a total
idiot, but most people will quickly ignore a poster who says nothing
worthwhile.

